    metaDescription: 'Perfect for Pre-K and Kindergarten, this sorting worksheet helps kids identify and categorize 2D shapes by color and type. Free printable logic activity.',
    learningObjectives: ['Identify 2D shapes (Circle, Square, Triangle)', 'Categorize objects by multiple attributes', 'Strengthen logical reasoning and visual discrimination'],
    richContent: "<article><h1 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 900; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.2;\">Shapes and Colors: The Foundation of Classification Logic</h1><p style=\"font-size: 1.125rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; line-height: 1.6;\">Discover our interactive 'Shapes and Colors Sorting' worksheets. Designed for pre-K and kindergarten, these activities build essential visual discrimination and logical reasoning skills by challenging students to categorize objects by multiple attributes. Free PDF download.</p><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Beyond Simple Recognition</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Learning to name a shape is a first step, but <strong>sorting by attribute</strong> is where mathematical logic begins. Our worksheets ask students to look at an object and decide: 'Is it red AND a circle?' This <strong>cross-attribute analysis</strong> is a critical precursor to scientific classification and computer logic. By manipulating these visual sets, young learners develop the cognitive flexibility required for all future analytical thinking.</p></section><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Key Developmental Milestones</h2><ul style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1.5rem;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Visual Discrimination:</strong> Training the eyes to spot small differences in shape and hue.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Decision Making:</strong> Evaluating an object against a set of rules to determine its correct category.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Fine Motor Skills:</strong> Precision coloring and marking reinforce the dexterity needed for writing.</li></ul></section><section><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Professional Primary Education Printables</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;\">Wizqo produces educator-approved resources that are free for personal and classroom use. Our PDFs are distraction-free and follow standard pediatric learning patterns to maximize engagement and retention. Every download includes a clear answer key for instant feedback. Start your child's logic journey today!</p></section></article>"
