    richContent: "<article><h1 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 900; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.2;\">Boundary Math: Perimeter of Rectangles</h1><p style=\"font-size: 1.125rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; line-height: 1.6;\">Measure the fence around the field with our 'Perimeter' worksheets. Designed for Grades 3 and 4, these activities help children understand <strong>linear boundaries</strong> and formulas (2L + 2W), building the spatial intuition needed for construction and design. Free PDF download for geometric arithmetic.</p><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">The Distance Around</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">How long is the border? Our worksheets help students move beyond simple counting to <strong>algebraic calculation</strong>. By identifying the length and width of four-sided shapes and adding all sides together, children build <strong>spatial reasoning</strong> and <strong>procedural stability</strong>. They learn the difference between area (inside) and perimeter (outside), a critical distinction for real-world projects like gardening or art framing. This practice is the essential precursor to high school geometry and understanding architectural blueprints. It turns abstract math into functional data that helps children build and create. This is the <strong>symbolic foundation</strong> of engineering sense and precise measurement. A must-have for every intermediate classroom.</p></section><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Mastery learning Goals</h2><ul style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1.5rem;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Unit Identification:</strong> always including the correct label (inches, cm) in results.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Formula Application:</strong> using 2L + 2W as a shortcut for efficiency.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Visual Estimation:</strong> predicting perimeter based on shape proportions.</li></ul></section><section><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Premier Academic Grade Visual Guides</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;\">Wizqo produces educator-approved resources that are free and instantly accessible. Our geometry sheets are high-resolution for professional visual study and follow standard curriculum paths for upper-elementary math. Every download includes a clear answer key. Measure your world today!</p></section></article>"
