    richContent: "<article><h1 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 900; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.2;\">Seeing the System: Base-Ten Blocks to 100</h1><p style=\"font-size: 1.125rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; line-height: 1.6;\">Visualize the structure of numbers with our 'Place Value Blocks' worksheets. Designed for Grades 1 and 2, these activities turn abstract digits into <strong>concrete lengths and groups</strong>, building the spatial intuition needed for multi-digit arithmetic. Free PDF download for visual math.</p><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">The Geometry of Arithmetic</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">A '4' in the tens-place is much larger than a '4' in the ones-place! Our worksheets help students move past rote counting to <strong>visual place-value logic</strong>. By identifying how many 'rods' (tens) and 'units' (ones) make up a value, children build <strong>conceptual stability</strong> and <strong>numerical scale</strong>. This practice is the essential precursor to addition with regrouping and understanding the metric system. It helps children develop a 'mental map' of numbers where larger values occupy more space, preventing common place-value errors in later grades. This is the <strong>symbolic foundation</strong> of base-ten fluency and logical calculation. A must-have for every primary math center.</p></section><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Early Math Milestones</h2><ul style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1.5rem;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Spatial Representation:</strong> seeing '32' as three distinct rods and two units.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Base-Ten Equivalence:</strong> realizing that 10 units stacked equal exactly one rod.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Visual Decoding:</strong> identifying numerical values from block-drawings on sight.</li></ul></section><section><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Premier Academic Grade Visuals</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;\">Wizqo produces educator-approved resources that are free and instantly accessible. Our block-visualization sheets are high-resolution for perfect visual clarity and follow standard pedagogical development paths for primary mathematics. Every download includes a clear answer key. Visualize your math today!</p></section></article>"
