    learningObjectives: ['Cite specific evidence from a digital text to solve a mystery', 'Develop advanced inference skills by connecting subtle narrative clues', 'Improve attention to detail and critical reading speed'],
    richContent: "<article><h1 style=\"font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: 900; color: #0f172a; margin-bottom: 1rem; line-height: 1.2;\">The Fact-Finder's Vault: Interactive Reading Detective</h1><p style=\"font-size: 1.125rem; color: #475569; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; line-height: 1.6;\">Discover the logic of 'Inference' with our 'Digital Mystery' experience. Designed for intermediate readers, this activity focuses on <strong>scanning text for evidence and cross-referencing clues to solve a case</strong>, building the foundational grit needed for research. Free digital access for future investigators.</p><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Investigating Between the Lines</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Get your magnifying glass ready! Our digital platform helps students move from simple reading to <strong>procedural evidence-based logic</strong>. Instead of just answering questions, students must harvest clues from the narrative and build a logical case to solve a high-stakes mystery. This develops <strong>foundational investigative awareness</strong> and the mental habit of 'rigorous detail-finding.' This practice is the essential precursor to high school lab reporting, understanding complex legal statutes, and professional intelligence analysis. It turns a standard paragraph into a clear, manageable map of investigative truth. This is the <strong>symbolic foundation</strong> of technical literacy and academic pride. The case is open - can you solve it?</p></section><section style=\"margin-bottom: 2rem;\"><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Investigative Mastery Goals</h2><ul style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6; padding-left: 1.5rem;\"><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Evidence Citation:</strong> correctly Identifying and highlighting specific sentences that prove or disprove a suspect's alibi.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Inference Rigor:</strong> practice connecting 'unspoken' clues (like a character's nervous reaction) to the broader narrative puzzle.</li><li style=\"margin-bottom: 0.5rem;\"><strong>Critical Review:</strong> understanding that every word on the page is a potential data-point for the final solution.</li></ul></section><section><h2 style=\"font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1rem;\">Premier Academic Grade Digital Assets</h2><p style=\"color: #475569; line-height: 1.6;\">Wizqo produces educator-vetted interactive resources that are free and instantly playable on all devices. Our detective games are high-fidelity for professional instruction and follow rigorous evidence-based development paths for reading excellence. Every session includes a unique evidence log. Find the truth today!</p></section></article>"
